# Mac mini runtime version pins — the desired state, in the repo.
#
# COMMITTED ON PURPOSE (not gitignored like services/*/.env): Renovate reads
# this file. `renovate.json` has a customManagers entry whose regex matches the
# `# renovate:` comment below plus the assignment under it. Reformat carefully —
# if the regex stops matching, Renovate goes quiet and you learn about the next
# Ollama release the way we learned about 0.33.3: by a model pull failing.
#
# See docs/MAC_MINI.md.

# The Ollama Mac app. Upgrading this REPLACES /Applications/Ollama.app, so it is
# never applied by the timer — a human runs `install.sh --upgrade-ollama`.
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=ollama/ollama
OLLAMA_VERSION=0.40.8

# ─── oMLX, the MLX inference server ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Installed from the macOS DMG attached to its GitHub release — NOT Homebrew,
# and that decision reverses the one this file's Ollama pin was born from, so
# it is worth the paragraph. MAC_MINI.md records Ollama being chosen "over
# Homebrew because it auto-updates and ships the CLI", and every mini incident
# since traces back to that sentence. The instinct to go the other way for oMLX
# is right. The tap defeats it for two measured reasons (2026-10-16):
#
#   1. The formula tracks release candidates. Its `url` was
#      v0.7.1rc1 while this pin says 0.7.0, and the tap carries no versioned
#      formulae to pin against — so `brew install` would ignore this file and
#      the pin would be decorative. That is the exact failure mode MAC_MINI.md
#      is about, reintroduced from the other side.
#   2. The kernels that matter need FULL XCODE, not the CLT. The formula's own
#      guard says so: "`metal` ships with Xcode, not the Command Line Tools."
#      Its CUSTOM_KERNELS list is bonsai, decode_fast, glm_moe_dsa, minimax_m3,
#      qwen35_prefill — and `qwen35_prefill` IS the prefill path for the
#      qwen3_5 hybrid architecture this box serves, with `decode_fast` the
#      decode path. A brew build without Xcode silently omits both, so it would
#      be a slower binary than the one the 2026-10-16 spike measured.
#
# The DMG ships those kernels precompiled (verified in the 0.7.0 bundle:
# omlx_qwen35_prefill_kernels.metallib, _nax.metallib,
# libomlx_qwen35_prefill_kernel_ops.dylib, omlx_decode_fast_kernels.metallib)
# and bundles its own CPython 3.11 and MLX, so it needs no toolchain at all.
#
# AND THE UPDATER OBJECTION IS ANSWERED STRUCTURALLY, not by a promise. The
# DMG does contain a GUI app with an in-app updater — but launchd runs
# `omlx-cli`, a DIFFERENT executable in the same bundle, and `strings` finds
# ZERO update-check symbols in it against 6 in the GUI binary (releases/latest,
# checkForUpdate and friends). install.sh therefore puts the bundle in
# ~/.coralstack/, not /Applications, so nothing can double-click it, and the
# reconcile reports it as a finding if a copy ever shows up there.
#
# AN "rc" TAG IS THIS PROJECT'S CURRENT RELEASE, NOT A PRERELEASE TO AVOID.
# Measured 2026-10-16: GitHub's own releases/latest endpoint returns
# v0.7.1rc1 with prerelease=false and draft=false, and the project's homepage
# download button points at releases/latest, so rc1 is what a new user gets.
#
# AN EARLIER DRAFT OF THIS FILE GOT THIS BACKWARDS and the mistake is worth
# recording, because it would have been invisible. It read prerelease=false on
# an "rc" tag as upstream mislabelling its prereleases, and leaned on
# `versioning: semver` in renovate.json to filter them out — "0.7.1rc1" is not
# valid semver, so Renovate cannot parse it and skips it. That filter was not
# protecting this box from instability. It was excluding the release the author
# considers current, and would have held this pin at 0.7.0 indefinitely while
# reporting everything as healthy. renovate.json now uses pep440 versioning,
# which understands rc tags, and excludes only .dev builds.
#
# What pinning an rc costs here is small and already graded: the mini is the
# one host where a bad update costs nothing (HARDWARE_FAILURE.md, "AI chat
# only ... nothing else depends on it"), which is the same risk inversion that
# makes model pulls automatic on this box and nowhere else.
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=jundot/omlx
OMLX_VERSION=0.7.1rc1

# The DMG's expected signer, asserted by `install.sh --install-omlx` before the
# bundle goes anywhere near the install path. Pinned rather than a SHA-256
# because upstream publishes no checksum file (the 0.7.0 release carries three
# wheels and two DMGs, nothing else) and because a signer identity SURVIVES a
# version bump where a hash does not — Renovate moves the pin above and would
# leave a stale hash behind as a false finding every single time.
#
# Measured from oMLX-0.7.0-macos26-27.dmg on 2026-10-16:
#   Authority=Developer ID Application: Heejun Kim (PSK5Q5T46L)
#   sha256=2e3bb06ac6ee7f50986ba1417e909d432ccd2be471db752a4a2d3b5651e3bce0
# Blank would mean log-only; it is set, so a different signer aborts the install.
OMLX_TEAM_ID=PSK5Q5T46L

# ─── Which runtime is expected to be SERVING ─────────────────────────────────
# `omlx` or `ollama`. This is the cutover switch and the rollback, and it is one
# reviewable line on purpose.
#
# IT EXISTS BECAUSE OF THE PERMANENT-RED TRAP. 48 GB cannot hold both runtimes'
# weights and caches (Ollama 18.2 GB growing to a 33 GB steady state, oMLX
# 15.45 GB plus a ~9.6 GB hot cache, against a ~44 GiB wired ceiling), so
# exactly one serves and the other sits installed as the rollback. A reconcile
# that did not know which would report the stopped one as "installed but not
# responding" every morning — a finding that can never be cleared, which
# MAC_MINI.md already paid 28 days to learn is indistinguishable from no alert.
#
# So the reconcile reads this and inverts: the primary must answer, and the
# OTHER one must NOT be serving. Two runtimes both answering is itself a
# finding, because that is the memory-thrash case.
MINI_PRIMARY_RUNTIME=omlx
